{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/781863-medicine-for-mortals","id":781863,"title":"Medicine for mortals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-07T15:06:56-08:00","id":781863,"title":"Medicine for mortals","content":"I was curious about how some medicines might work in the WoD for mortals. While many supernaturals and some endowed hunters have some ability to let them heal quickly, mortals often have to rely on mundane medicines for slow healing. In particular I was wondering about the mechanics of pain killers.<br /> <br /> Let's say you play a VASCU agent who gets bashing damage for using a low level Teleinformatics ability. In game it is said that this is represented as being a headache, and OTC pain killers are known for generally being able to get rid of headaches. Well, if said agent were to take a couple of Aspirin, would the 1 bashing be healed at the end of the scene or after an hour because the 1 B comes in the form of a headache? Also seeing as most forms of bashing damage aren't healed by hawking Tylenol, say you got a bruise from being punched, would pain killers instead be able to downplay damage penalties? Like OTC pain killers could negate one damage penalty after an hour in game while prescription pain killers can negate two or three damage penalties almost instantly?<br /> <br /> What about quick clotting agents? Like those powders you pour on open wounds to make them clot instantly and stop the bleeding? How would those work in game, mechanistically?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","name":"Zolace","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T15:15:52-08:00","id":781871,"title":"","content":"In general, I run with the notion that damage heals normally but pain can inflict penalties that painkillers negate. Creatures that heal fast don't need them, but those that can't, do.<br /> <br /> In general, standard medicine is very good when the ST is like &quot;you took a hell of a beating. That's at least a -1 on all actions from the pain.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T16:14:00-08:00","id":781917,"title":"","content":"Okay. Would it heal a point of bashing if the bashing was present purely as a headache though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","name":"Zolace","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T17:03:58-08:00","id":781949,"title":"","content":"Bashing heals at the rate Bashing heals regardless of of how it is represented. Painkillers negate wound and pain penalties, they don't heal.<br /> <br /> Also, from an actual medical perspective, your headache has a physiological cause. It's not just sourceless pain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T17:31:19-08:00","id":781962,"title":"","content":"Okay. What about that quick clotting powder I mentioned? How do the mechanics of bleeding out and stopping bleeding work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","name":"Zolace","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T17:44:50-08:00","id":781972,"title":"","content":"There are rules for stopping bleed. Clotting powder can be the thing that allows you to try it at all when you don't have surgical tools or bandages at hand. Or might allow you to justify using the medicine skill on yourself to stop bleeding, assuming you have a way to stay conscious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}